  message: "SHIPPED as PR #961 (merged). The false dead-end marker is off fmt.Fprintf and\nfmt.Fprintln, the entries are kept as tombstones, and the terminating set is\npinned as a 37-entry census with its own controls (fmt.Printf and log.Println\nMUST still terminate, so a blanket change fails rather than passing).\n\nThis closes the LIVE defect. The item stays open on the narrowed residual it\nwas corrected to: there is no param_to_param, so the flow INTO arg 0 can be\nrefused but not MODELLED. Refusing is correct and safe; modelling buys recall\nand should be designed with WI-famig's param_to_calls rather than bolted on.\n\nVerified after merge: 27087 passed on the full suite (the targeted slice\nselected ONE file -- INV-dohoj), ratchet 669 delta +0."  # 032a
